  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Hokuto tried to improve his Necromancy, but the task was beyond 
his natural aptitude.
  With the coming of the early summer season Hokuto worked on his Necromancy 
but was thwarted in his self-improvement efforts.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  Hokuto 
practiced his Necromancy well but could not improve his skill in Necromancy.
  In fall, Hokuto discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Hokuto invented nothing worthy 
of note in his sagely researches.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Hokuto for this year.

  Mugai (#3) Treated with Hokuto, but Hokuto did not react favorably to his 
friendly overtures.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will see the 
wisdom of Treating.


  Here is the financial report for Hokuto's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Hokuto was left with 16 gold in 
the treasury.


